---Your authored or assigned project Trails
---
---Project Trails you authored or that are assigned to you and may read through project authority or a repository in their stored scope, most recently updated first by default. Discovery, authorship, and assignment alone never grant access. An assignment matches your account ID, or your linked GitHub login for legacy assignments; each Trail appears once. Takes the same filters as a project's Trail list (status, phase, type, priority, author, assignee, their _not exclusions, and search), which only narrow your Trails, plus project_id and sort, with cursor/per_page pagination. A cursor is bound to your account and to the filters and sort that produced it. If Core cannot resolve your GitHub login, authored and account-assigned Trails are still listed and meta.partial carries unresolved_caller_login. If the stored Change readiness read fails, building Trails return `changes: []` and meta.partial carries change_readiness_unavailable; a project catalog failure returns 503.
---
---`GET /api/v1/me/project-trails`
---@param input? entire.me.ListMyProjectTrailsRequest
---@return entire.me.MeProjectTrailsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_my_project_trails(input) end

